Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.40,0:00:14.36,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,That’s some good cake.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.80,0:00:23.00,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,What a pathetic form…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.46,0:00:31.76,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,…Iorogi.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:00.00,KM,{Title TS,0000,0000,0000,,Silver Eyes
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.36,0:02:19.32,KM,Marina,0000,0000,0000,,Ah! It’s Kobato-chan!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.70,0:02:21.57,KM,Toshihiko,0000,0000,0000,,Good morning, Kobato-chan!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.57,0:02:23.05,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Good morning!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.45,0:02:27.33,KM,Marina,0000,0000,0000,,Kobato-chan, can I tie a ribbon on the puppy?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.83,0:02:29.12,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Puppy?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.67,0:02:31.46,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Do you mean Ioryogi-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.83,0:02:34.50,KT,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Come on! Gimme a break here!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.50,0:02:36.57,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Yes! Please do!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.57,0:02:43.47,KM,Marina,0000,0000,0000,,He’s cute!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.47,0:02:46.16,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Yes! Ioryogi-san likes it!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.16,0:02:48.35,KT,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Who the hell would like this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.69,0:02:53.36,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Good morning!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.36,0:02:55.19,KM,Sayaka,0000,0000,0000,,Good morning, Kobato-chan.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.48,0:02:56.98,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,I hope we’ll have a good day today.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.98,0:02:58.03,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.16,0:03:06.12,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Well, I’m off, Ioryogi-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.21,0:03:16.09,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,Why does she carry that thing around with her?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.47,0:03:18.67,KM,Sayaka,0000,0000,0000,,I’m sure it’s precious to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.97,0:03:28.45,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,Time to cook, time to cook…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:00.00,KM,{Door TS,0000,0000,0000,,Bear’s Baumkuchen Shop
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.81,0:03:31.46,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,…tasty and delicious baumkuchen.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.94,0:03:33.69,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Cook them, cook them.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.69,0:03:36.46,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,That’s right, bake and cook them!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.23,0:03:40.97,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,The bear in the woods will be baking… them.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.91,0:03:44.09,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Annoying.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.41,0:03:46.95,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Hurry up and get in here, Ginsei!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.91,0:03:53.33,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,He’s not here, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.33,0:03:54.96,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.96,0:03:57.02,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Then what did you come here for?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.50,0:03:59.30,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,I just want to know something.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.81,0:04:02.03,KM,,0000,0000,0000,,What is he thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.28,0:04:03.97,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,Why ask me that?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.81,0:04:05.53,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Fine then.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.39,0:04:10.81,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,The reason we look the way we do is\Nbecause of the dweller of the spirit world.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.81,0:04:12.10,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,Why suddenly bring{\fscx200}-
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.10,0:04:14.29,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,So how did it all begin?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.69,0:04:15.94,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,The Celestial World.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.94,0:04:17.23,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,The Human World.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.23,0:04:18.44,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,The Nether World.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.44,0:04:20.05,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,And then the Spirit World.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.94,0:04:26.80,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,The only ones not aware of those separate\Nworlds are the humans living in their world.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.82,0:04:32.29,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(0,400)}The Celestial World has\Nangels under God’s command.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.91,0:04:37.83,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(0,480)}The Nether World contains\Ndemons under Satan’s command.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.59,0:04:45.01,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(0,700)}We of the Spirit World are under\Nthe command of the Spirit Master.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.18,0:04:49.22,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Those separate worlds\Nshare a non-aggression pact.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.22,0:04:51.04,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,But that idiot Ioryogi…
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.73,0:04:57.06,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,All right, that {\i1}somewhat idiotic{\i0} Ioryogi.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.56,0:05:02.15,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,All this happened because he waged a war against the Celestial World.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.34,0:05:08.18,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,The reason Ioryogi started a\Nwar with the Celestial World…
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.70,0:05:12.37,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,…was because there was\Nsomething there he wanted dearly.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.08,0:05:14.12,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,However…
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.62,0:05:16.54,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,He failed to obtain it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.25,0:05:18.33,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.33,0:05:22.86,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,He could have done what the son of\NSatan would have done and stolen it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.84,0:05:25.84,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,We ended up losing,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.84,0:05:29.12,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,and he was made into a stuffed animal as\Npenance for breaking the non-aggression pact.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.47,0:05:32.39,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,I’m now a bear working in a baumkuchen shop.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.39,0:05:35.06,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,And Zuishou is now some strange little bird.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.56,0:05:40.54,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Even God has only so much patience.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.27,0:05:46.63,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,We were all willing participants, but the\Nringleader got the brunt of the punishment.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.53,0:05:50.60,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,So how can Iorogi return to the Spirit World?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.53,0:05:55.93,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,Until that child’s wish is granted, Ioryogi will remain in that form…
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.93,0:05:58.17,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,…unable to return to the Spirit World.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.17,0:05:59.44,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,Wish?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.46,0:06:04.34,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,She must heal the grieving\Nhearts belonging to the humans.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.76,0:06:09.55,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,When she fills up that bottle, her wish will be granted.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.39,0:06:13.28,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,It was God’s will for him to assist her.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.81,0:06:17.56,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,I don’t know what’s going on in his head.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.06,0:06:23.36,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,But I’ll tell you this much: after\Nhe arrived in the Human World…
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.36,0:06:28.30,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,No, after he ended up\Nwith that child, he changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.15,0:06:31.45,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,So let’s just leave him alone for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.45,0:06:32.60,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,And you can have this{\fscx200}-
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.54,0:06:37.66,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Geez!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.62,0:06:41.25,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,And it tastes good too.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.88,0:06:46.17,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,I hope none of my old comrades see me like this!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.88,0:06:50.45,KM,Sayaka,0000,0000,0000,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.23,0:07:06.94,KM,Hoshihiko,0000,0000,0000,,Come tag me, I’m right here!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.94,0:07:08.94,KM,Doumoto,0000,0000,0000,,Kobato-chan, good morning!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.07,0:07:11.66,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Doumoto-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.28,0:07:14.92,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Why are you at the preschool?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.92,0:07:17.12,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,I have a little business with Kiyokazu.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.00,0:07:21.08,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,Everyone, time for lunch!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.08,0:07:22.83,KM,,0000,0000,0000,,Wash your hands and go inside!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.83,0:07:24.13,KM,kids,0000,0000,0000,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.13,0:07:24.69,KM,Doumoto,0000,0000,0000,,Kiyokazu!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.50,0:07:28.19,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,What are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.19,0:07:32.07,KM,Doumoto,0000,0000,0000,,I think you should come to the\Nseminar today, so I came to invite you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.39,0:07:34.32,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,I’m not going.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.32,0:07:36.56,KM,Doumoto,0000,0000,0000,,But it’s the class you wanted!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.06,0:07:39.28,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Excuse me, what’s a “seminar”?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.28,0:07:41.65,KM,Doumoto,0000,0000,0000,,A seminar class. At college.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.65,0:07:44.40,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Ah, so it’s for college learning!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.40,0:07:44.83,KM,Doumoto,0000,0000,0000,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.36,0:07:49.82,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,You were absent the last time,\Nso you should really come today.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.82,0:07:52.24,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Please go, Fujimoto-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.24,0:07:54.24,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,Can’t do it. Busy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.74,0:08:00.12,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Fujimoto-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.12,0:08:01.00,KM,Doumoto,0000,0000,0000,,Kobato-chan…
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.46,0:08:04.40,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,It’s all right. I have an idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.13,0:08:13.08,KM,Sayaka,0000,0000,0000,,You’ve done enough for today. You have an important seminar this afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.08,0:08:14.53,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,Sayaka-san…
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.01,0:08:18.89,KM,Doumoto,0000,0000,0000,,I've also come here to help several times.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.89,0:08:20.79,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,So I knew just what to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.13,0:08:25.69,KM,Sayaka,0000,0000,0000,,The kids will be taking afternoon naps soon, and I have Kobato-chan here to help. We’ll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.69,0:08:26.86,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,But…
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.86,0:08:27.81,KM,Sayaka,0000,0000,0000,,Fujimoto-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.48,0:08:30.57,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,You’re always a real lifesaver.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.03,0:08:34.05,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,But I still want you to attend your college.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.70,0:08:36.99,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.95,0:08:39.20,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.49,0:08:41.33,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,He’s obeying her.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.33,0:08:45.44,KM,Doumoto,0000,0000,0000,,He only listens to what Sayaka-sensei says.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.13,0:08:50.42,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Dress {\i1}me{\i0} up as some\Nfairy-tale character, will they!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.07,0:09:13.57,KM,Doumoto,0000,0000,0000,,See you, Kobato-chan. I’ll come again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.57,0:09:16.20,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Yes! Please come again!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.20,0:09:18.49,KM,Doumoto,0000,0000,0000,,See you later!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.41,0:09:23.70,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Take care!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.58,0:09:31.71,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(0,1200)} I’ll do my best to fill in for Fujimoto-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.06,0:09:44.85,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Oh, that’s amazing!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.77,0:09:56.65,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Dammit! That Fujimoto punk\Nmade the knot too tight to get off!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.31,0:10:28.35,KM,Sayaka,0000,0000,0000,,I can’t thank you enough for today.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.35,0:10:30.71,KM,Sayaka,0000,0000,0000,,Your coming here really helped us out.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.71,0:10:32.52,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,O-Oh, you’re welcome!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.52,0:10:34.75,KM,Sayaka,0000,0000,0000,,Get some rest once you return home.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.75,0:10:35.90,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.94,0:10:40.01,KM,Sayaka,0000,0000,0000,,That ribbon looks good on Ioryogi-chan.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.32,0:10:44.83,KT,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi… chan?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.83,0:10:48.08,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.08,0:10:49.77,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,I’ll see you tomorrow!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.09,0:11:00.72,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,It’s still pretty hot out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.89,0:11:09.77,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,A leafy place might be cooler.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.86,0:11:17.69,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,This feels better. Right, Ioryogi-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.41,0:11:25.39,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,That hurts! What do you think you’re doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.83,0:11:29.25,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,You were all scrunched up right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.04,0:11:31.96,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Know why?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.96,0:11:34.29,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Are you perhaps hungry?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.26,0:11:47.60,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Kobato.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.52,0:11:52.64,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,The seasons are passing us by.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.64,0:11:57.73,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,You didn’t come here just\Nto help out at a preschool.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.57,0:12:07.37,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,But I had to work hard filling in for\NFujimoto-san when he wasn’t there today.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.37,0:12:08.81,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,That’s what I’m talking about.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.14,0:12:10.91,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,You have to do what you’re {\i1}supposed{\i0} to be doing!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.67,0:12:19.69,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,If you don’t fill this bottle up\Nquickly, your wish won’t be granted.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.60,0:12:31.73,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Ginsei?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.73,0:12:33.91,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Is that a friend of yours, Ioryogi-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.99,0:12:49.16,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.00,0:12:53.02,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,So that’s her?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.87,0:12:55.79,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Kobato!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.52,0:13:18.46,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san…
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.76,0:13:46.70,KM,Kohaku,0000,0000,0000,,Huh? What’s that?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.31,0:13:59.85,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Bastard. If you break that, I’ll make you regret it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.90,0:14:01.73,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.27,0:14:07.61,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Why do you remain in the\NHuman World in that form?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.03,0:14:13.20,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Because it’s something I have to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.26,0:14:26.78,KM,Zuishou,0000,0000,0000,,Genko-sama!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.92,0:14:31.05,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,Zuishou! Don’t flap your wings in here!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.05,0:14:32.76,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,You’ll get your feathers in the batter!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.76,0:14:36.60,KM,Zuishou,0000,0000,0000,,I hear what you’re saying, but I’m still a bird.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.60,0:14:39.50,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,I know, I know. So, what’s up?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.50,0:14:41.23,KM,Zuishou,0000,0000,0000,,Oh, that’s right!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.23,0:14:45.65,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,I think that slavedriving selfish\Nguy who’s now a stuffed animal,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.65,0:14:50.76,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,and that other guy that had a violent past are about to enter a critical situation!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.24,0:14:53.49,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,Oh, is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.49,0:14:54.87,KM,Zuishou,0000,0000,0000,,Huh? That’s it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.87,0:14:57.70,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,Here, take this with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.70,0:14:59.79,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Give it to the loser as a get-well gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.79,0:15:01.21,KM,Zuishou,0000,0000,0000,,Are you sure we should leave them alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.21,0:15:04.59,KM,Zuishou,0000,0000,0000,,Their fight will be of epic proportions!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.59,0:15:07.11,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,Neither of us could stop them even if we tried.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.42,0:15:11.11,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi originally took that guy under his wing.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.43,0:15:13.80,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,He even gave him his name.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.80,0:15:15.74,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Since his eye is silver in color,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.14,0:15:18.39,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,he was called Ginsei {\fscx200}-{\r} Quicksilver.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.35,0:15:22.00,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,No matter the circumstances, that’s how it’ll be with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.40,0:15:26.57,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Or so I thought. But then\Nthey began exchanging blows.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.57,0:15:27.61,KM,Zuishou,0000,0000,0000,,And how.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.69,0:15:30.95,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,He took him in and gave him his name.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.95,0:15:34.03,KM,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,So now he maintains his obsession with Ioryogi.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.47,0:15:38.10,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,They are the only ones who can settle their feud.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.01,0:15:55.53,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Give back that bottle!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.10,0:15:58.56,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,Why not take it yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.56,0:16:00.18,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,“Ioryogi-san.”
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.60,0:16:04.06,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Keep it up if you wanna get fried!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.86,0:16:13.36,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,You’re not going to pin anyone down while in that form.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.36,0:16:14.39,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,You son of a…
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.70,0:16:18.53,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,Simply pathetic. Your appearance. Your name.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.53,0:16:20.39,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,Who {\i1}is{\i0} “Ioryogi” anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.96,0:16:24.71,KP,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(0,780)} “Io… ryo?”
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.04,0:16:29.92,KP,Iorogi,0000,0000,0000,,“Iorogi!”
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.84,0:16:33.30,KP,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,“Io… {\i1}ryo{\i0}gi.”
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.01,0:16:35.64,KP,Iorogi,0000,0000,0000,,It’s “Iorogi!”
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.64,0:16:38.14,KP,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,“I… o… ryogi?”
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.14,0:16:40.52,KP,Iorogi,0000,0000,0000,,No! It’s “Ioryogi!”
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.52,0:16:41.27,KP,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.39,0:16:44.52,KP,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Yes! Ioryogi-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.19,0:16:50.40,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,I grew to like the name she calls me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.28,0:16:52.92,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Now hand back the bottle.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.74,0:16:56.53,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,Say you’ll come back to the Spirit World.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.53,0:16:59.08,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,I told you I need to be here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.08,0:17:00.95,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,So I’m not going back.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.95,0:17:02.91,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Not until I finish my job.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.58,0:17:07.04,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,You’re talking about that wish?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.00,0:17:11.25,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,What does that girl mean to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.92,0:17:15.53,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,That girl…
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.34,0:17:19.28,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,…has put me through a lot of pain and suffering.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.60,0:17:24.89,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,Then we can just eliminate her.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.89,0:17:25.94,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.94,0:17:31.80,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,If we remove the girl, there won’t be any wish, and you will have to return to the Spirit World.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.61,0:17:34.82,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,That’s what the old you would do.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.28,0:17:37.30,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Got that right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.78,0:17:41.20,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,She’s one clumsy oaf, without a lick of common sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.78,0:17:43.83,KP,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,I will do my best!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.83,0:17:48.21,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,She’s always putting off\Nwhat she came here to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.21,0:17:53.25,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,And she works herself to death for\Nother people without even being asked.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.05,0:17:54.82,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,But still…
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.80,0:18:01.18,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,I can’t hate how she’s such a hopeless screw-up.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.10,0:18:09.06,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,You didn’t answer me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.06,0:18:12.07,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,You’re squeezing out the stuffing, you bastard!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.07,0:18:16.36,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,If she doesn’t fill the bottle, her wish won’t come true.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.03,0:18:18.34,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Ginsei!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.86,0:18:20.14,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,In that case…
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.36,0:18:21.72,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Once we take this away…
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.37,0:18:23.45,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.37,0:18:31.58,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,Right now you’re in no position to give orders!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.75,0:18:34.96,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Ginsei!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.34,0:18:36.51,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,I beg you!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.80,0:18:41.30,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Give me back the bottle.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.10,0:18:46.64,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Without it, Kobato will…
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.89,0:18:49.06,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,I beg you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.27,0:18:55.98,KP,Genko,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(0,740)} …after he ended up with that child, he changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.95,0:19:00.45,KM,Ginsei,0000,0000,0000,,You’re begging me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.66,0:19:06.70,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,The old you would never\Neven dream of doing that.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.22,0:19:26.51,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Hurry and accomplish your goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.68,0:19:29.93,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Ginsei…
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.52,0:19:36.94,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.94,0:19:39.92,KM,Kohaku,0000,0000,0000,,Kobato-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.92,0:19:41.57,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Kohaku-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.57,0:19:43.53,KM,Kohaku,0000,0000,0000,,What’s the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.53,0:19:46.05,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san has gone missing!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.08,0:19:51.31,KM,Kohaku,0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san is presently in Sakura Park…
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.00,0:19:55.54,KM,"Ginsei",0000,0000,0000,,Come on, try to catch me!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.54,0:19:57.22,KM,"Ioryogi",0000,0000,0000,,Why you…!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.22,0:20:04.09,KM,Kohaku,0000,0000,0000,,Since he was playfully scampering after a friend from the Spirit World, I didn’t call out to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.39,0:20:07.93,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Sakura Park? Thank you very much!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.89,0:20:11.08,KM,Kohaku,0000,0000,0000,,You’re very welcome!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.86,0:20:25.11,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Crap, this useless body of mine!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.11,0:20:27.28,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Still, having come this far…
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.15,0:20:44.20,KT,'',0000,0000,0000,,That hurts, jackass!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.97,0:20:47.30,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.51,0:20:54.37,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san! Where are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.14,0:20:57.40,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.06,0:20:59.13,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.94,0:21:02.38,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Fujimoto-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.95,0:21:06.03,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.03,0:21:07.70,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.05,0:21:10.91,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Thank goodness, Ioryogi-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.52,0:21:15.54,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Thank you very much for finding Ioryogi-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.25,0:21:17.25,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,Sure…
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.04,0:21:21.13,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san got himself lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.75,0:21:22.84,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,Lost?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.84,0:21:25.93,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,I’m really glad that Ioryogi-san is okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.59,0:21:29.26,KM,Fujimoto,0000,0000,0000,,So, this thing is that important to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.97,0:21:31.22,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.22,0:21:34.48,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san and I are always together!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.44,0:21:39.44,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,This is good!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.36,0:21:44.74,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,That bear sure knows what I go for.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.72,0:21:54.04,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,It looks really good on you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.04,0:21:55.44,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Why you little…!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.44,0:21:56.65,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.25,0:22:03.36,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Thank you for getting back the bottle for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.36,0:22:04.96,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,I’m really grateful.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.72,0:22:08.05,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Dobato!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.76,0:22:11.39,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Minus 200 points!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.14,0:22:16.89,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Why did you let your precious bottle get stolen?! You’re slacking off!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.52,0:22:19.37,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,I’m sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.06,0:22:25.61,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,What is this? Dress-up day?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.61,0:22:28.20,KM,'',0000,0000,0000,,Wherever I go, people are tying ribbons on me!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.70,0:22:32.91,KP,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san and I are always together!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.75,0:22:40.08,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Ioryogi-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.08,0:22:41.25,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.25,0:22:43.75,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,You really do look good with ribbons!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.75,0:22:44.84,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,No, I don’t!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.84,0:22:48.84,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Of course you do! Look, if we tie this one on here…
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.84,0:22:50.05,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,Stop that!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.05,0:22:51.76,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Then if we tie another one on here…
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.76,0:22:53.64,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,I told you to stop, dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.64,0:22:55.68,KM,Dobato,0000,0000,0000,,Oh, and let’s tie one more…
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.68,0:22:58.68,KM,Ioryogi,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(0,1700)} Now I can’t even talk!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:00.00,KM,{Next Episode TS,0000,0000,0000,,The Angel and The Protector}
